WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.500 --> 00:00:04.800
Build a headless browser, or not?

2
00:00:04.800 --> 00:00:08.100
It would cost a model its memory.

3
00:00:08.100 --> 00:00:10.300
The plan refused to guess.

4
00:00:10.300 --> 00:00:13.700
So: where do prices actually live?

5
00:00:13.700 --> 00:00:16.200
Cheapest rung first.

6
00:00:16.200 --> 00:00:19.300
One mistake would answer zero.

7
00:00:19.300 --> 00:00:23.300
Script contents are removed, not untagged.

8
00:00:23.300 --> 00:00:26.300
And a number is not a price.

9
00:00:26.300 --> 00:00:30.200
A currency marker next to it, or nothing.

10
00:00:30.200 --> 00:00:33.500
Twenty-eight real pricing pages.

11
00:00:33.500 --> 00:00:36.500
Most simply print the price.

12
00:00:36.500 --> 00:00:40.000
The leftover is two things, not one.

13
00:00:40.000 --> 00:00:43.800
No browser renders a price nobody wrote.

14
00:00:43.800 --> 00:00:47.100
Two pages were there to catch us.

15
00:00:47.100 --> 00:00:49.900
One did, on the first run.

16
00:00:49.900 --> 00:00:52.900
So the browser is not built.

17
00:00:52.900 --> 00:00:55.600
The memory stays with the models.
